From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nss-ppe: port the PPE core driver to Linux 6.12

qca-nss-ppe's core module (drv/ppe_drv, built with ppe-drv=y)
compiles with -Werror, so the following 6.12 API changes are fatal:

  ppe_drv.c:3061  platform_driver.remove now returns void (6.11)
  ppe_drv.c (15x) proc_handler takes const struct ctl_table * (6.10)
  ppe_drv.c:4161  dsa_slave_dev_check() renamed to dsa_user_dev_check()
  ppe_drv.c:4406  strlcpy() removed, strscpy() is the replacement
  ppe_drv.c       -Wmissing-prototypes (6.10): four file-local helpers
  exception.h     const on a scalar return type is ignored (-Werror)

Classification:

  removed/changed API     platform remove, ctl_table const, strlcpy,
                          dsa_slave_dev_check
  mainline equivalent     dsa_user_dev_check(), strscpy()
  must shim               none; the four helpers get internal linkage
                          because no caller exists outside ppe_drv.c and
                          none of them is EXPORT_SYMBOL'd

ppe_drv_l4_checksum_exception_enable() and ppe_drv_mac_lrn_exception_en()
are also made static: they are only referenced from the local sysctl
table, and being static they no longer need a prototype.

Only drv/ppe_drv is built by this configuration.  The optional PPE
submodules (ppe_vp, ppe_qdisc, ppe_tun, ppe_ds, ppe_rule) carry the same
ctl_table signature and were not compiled or fixed here; their status is
UNVERIFIED.
